.SH NAME
lmm-profile - Manage mod profiles


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBlmm profile [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage mod profiles for organizing different mod configurations.

.PP
Profiles allow you to maintain different sets of mods for the same game.
For example, you might have a "vanilla plus" profile and a "total conversion" profile.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for profile


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	config directory (default: ~/.config/lmm)

.PP
\fB--data\fP=""
	data directory (default: ~/.local/share/lmm)

.PP
\fB-g\fP, \fB--game\fP=""
	game ID to operate on

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	output in JSON format (list, status, search, update, conflicts, verify, mod show, source list)

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	disable colored output (NO_COLOR env is also honored)

.PP
\fB--no-hooks\fP[=false]
	disable all hooks

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	verbose output


